Package: dotmatch
Title: R Interface to DotMatch (Deterministic Short-DNA Assignment)
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("DotMatch Contributors", email = "donncha@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides R wrappers around the Python dotmatch package via
    reticulate. Enables Bioconductor and tidyverse users to use DotMatch's
    exact, ambiguity-aware assignment for CRISPR guides, feature barcodes,
    inline barcodes, and other known-target assays directly from R.
    For production scale, the native CLI is recommended; these helpers
    support interactive analysis and small-to-medium data from R.
License: Apache License 2.0
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: 
    reticulate
Suggests:
    SingleCellExperiment,
    SummarizedExperiment,
    data.table,
    testthat
RoxygenNote: 7.2.3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
